---
// prose + pipeline diagram: AI shipped into products, not just AI-assisted coding
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="ai-heading">
  <div class="wrap section-grid">
    <p class="kicker"><span class="no">03</span>$ cat ai.md</p>
    <div class="ai-grid">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2 id="ai-heading" class="sr-only">AI engineering</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          I don't just use AI to write code. <span class="accent-text"
            >I ship AI inside the product — and make it behave.</span
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          The AI features I've built run in production for real users: chat support on OpenAI
          that handles profile completion, job-matching questions, and referral guidance — and a
          matching pipeline where jobs and candidates become embeddings, Qdrant does the vector
          search, and scored matches flow back into the platform.
        </p>
        <p>
          Production AI is boundary engineering. A model is an unreliable dependency like any
          other, so the real work lives at the edges: structured outputs validated before they
          touch data, fallbacks for when the model is wrong or slow, and observability so a bad
          answer is a bug report instead of a mystery.
        </p>
        <p class="soft">
          Currently going deeper down the stack — RAG pipelines, embedding strategy, and
          self-hosted models.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="diagram-panel reveal">
        <figcaption class="sr-only">
          The matching pipeline: jobs and candidates are embedded via OpenAI, searched in Qdrant,
          and scored matches ship to production.
        </figcaption>
        <pre class="diagram" aria-hidden="true">
  job post         candidate
      │                │
      └───►<span class="d-key"> openai </span>◄───┘
          embeddings
               │
               ▼
 ┌─<span class="d-key"> qdrant · vector search </span>─┐
 │   similarity, not         │
 │   keyword matching        │
 └─────────────┬─────────────┘
               ▼
<span class="d-key">  chat support (openai)</span>
   ├─ profile completion
   ├─ job-match questions
   └─ referral guidance
               │
               ▼
  ship ──► production <span class="d-live">● live</span>
<span class="d-note">  # real users, every day</span></pre>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ai-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .ai-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 0.95rem + 0.6vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .accent-text {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .prose p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .prose p + p {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .soft {
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .diagram-panel {
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--panel);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .diagram {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .d-key {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .d-live {
    color: oklch(75% 0.18 145);
  }

  .d-note {
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
